{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21880366",
      "title": "Reusability Concepts",
      "lectureOrder": 311,
      "videoOrder": 277,
      "sourceHash": "9a0a93c7e0d5db53d56b3de7682703229c2ddcc2359a6d92f66583005e3e3709",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 3.3,
          "en": "For this, I, again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.3,
          "end": 6.03,
          "en": "prepared a little starting project for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.03,
          "end": 7.58,
          "en": "It is a simple project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.58,
          "end": 10.45,
          "en": "which you can start as always with NPM install",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.45,
          "end": 11.68,
          "en": "and NPM run surf.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 11.68,
          "end": 15.17,
          "en": "And when you do so you will see this on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.17,
          "end": 18.04,
          "en": "We've got two dummy components here for adding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.04,
          "end": 20.02,
          "en": "and deleting a user, presumably.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.02,
          "end": 23.04,
          "en": "And when we click add user, we open a,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.04,
          "end": 25.86,
          "en": "an alert, a model with add a user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 25.86,
          "end": 29.257,
          "en": "and the text asking us whether we want to add a user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.257,
          "end": 31.88,
          "en": "and we can close this by clicking on the backdrop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 31.88,
          "end": 34.2,
          "en": "or by clicking on the close button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.2,
          "end": 36.05,
          "en": "And when we click on delete user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 36.05,
          "end": 40.01,
          "en": "we see almost the same dialogue, the same alert,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.01,
          "end": 43.53,
          "en": "but with a different content, a different text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.53,
          "end": 47.16,
          "en": "and therefore here in App Vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.16,
          "end": 49.88,
          "en": "I'm adding add and delete user these two components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.88,
          "end": 51.36,
          "en": "And in these components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 51.36,
          "end": 55.24,
          "en": "I have my alert component added as a local component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 55.24,
          "end": 57.69,
          "en": "actually in both components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 57.69,
          "end": 60.28,
          "en": "we could add it as a global component as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 60.28,
          "end": 62.93,
          "en": "but here I went for the same component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 62.93,
          "end": 67.01,
          "en": "added as a local component into different components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 67.01,
          "end": 71,
          "en": "And besides that add user and delete user are very similar.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 71,
          "end": 73.43,
          "en": "They've got pretty much the same logic in them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 73.43,
          "end": 75.88,
          "en": "but they got a different template, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 75.88,
          "end": 79.17,
          "en": "because that is where these components differ.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 79.17,
          "end": 81.6,
          "en": "And that already brings us to the core topic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 81.6,
          "end": 85.32,
          "en": "of this module, reusing logic and code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 85.32,
          "end": 87.33,
          "en": "And for that, let's start simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 87.33,
          "end": 91.03999999999999,
          "en": "What can we reuse in a Vue application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 91.03999999999999,
          "end": 94.713,
          "en": "or in any web application, if we think about it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 95.96000000000001,
          "end": 100.03999999999999,
          "en": "Well, for one that's of course our HTML structure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.03999999999999,
          "end": 102.83,
          "en": "and styling, this is something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.83,
          "end": 104.92,
          "en": "which we often reuse on our page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.92,
          "end": 108.09,
          "en": "We often have different parts on our page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 108.09,
          "end": 112.35,
          "en": "which actually use the same HTML structure and styling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 112.35,
          "end": 115.88300000000001,
          "en": "Think about list items where every list item looks the same,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117,
          "end": 120.58,
          "en": "but we also often want to reuse logic and events,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 120.58,
          "end": 122.29,
          "en": "which we might want to handle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 122.29,
          "end": 126.38,
          "en": "And that's exactly why we have this components concept with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 126.38,
          "end": 129.25,
          "en": "this core concept built into Vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 129.25,
          "end": 133.28,
          "en": "we have a powerful way of encapsulating structure,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 133.28,
          "end": 135.89,
          "en": "styling and logic into a component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 135.89,
          "end": 139.56,
          "en": "and then using that component wherever we needed on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 139.56,
          "end": 143.48,
          "en": "the page, and thanks to props and slots,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 143.48,
          "end": 147.363,
          "en": "we can still customize this component to a certain extent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 148.65,
          "end": 149.483,
          "en": "And in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.483,
          "end": 152.72,
          "en": "that's what I'm doing in this mini app here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.72,
          "end": 157.02,
          "en": "The user alerts component is a reusable component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 157.02,
          "end": 160.78,
          "en": "which defines the structure and styling for a backdrop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 160.78,
          "end": 162.27,
          "en": "and the overlay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 162.27,
          "end": 166.3,
          "en": "And then I'm using this component in both the delete user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 166.3,
          "end": 168.683,
          "en": "as well as the add user component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 169.66,
          "end": 171.82,
          "en": "And these components themselves, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 171.82,
          "end": 176.07,
          "en": "are also encapsulated pieces of HTML code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 176.07,
          "end": 178.203,
          "en": "and logic attached to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 179.12,
          "end": 182.32,
          "en": "And that is really the idea of components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 182.32,
          "end": 186.5,
          "en": "We have HTML structure, styling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 186.5,
          "end": 189.14,
          "en": "and possibly also some logic like here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 189.14,
          "end": 193.06,
          "en": "for emitting this close event in the user alert component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 193.06,
          "end": 197.163,
          "en": "which is all encapsulated into one reusable building block.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 198.24,
          "end": 199.87,
          "en": "Now that's nothing new though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 199.87,
          "end": 204.42000000000002,
          "en": "We worked with components for hours and hours already at",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 204.42000000000002,
          "end": 206.49,
          "en": "this point in the course and they offered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 206.49,
          "end": 207.56,
          "en": "that's nothing new,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 207.56,
          "end": 210.59,
          "en": "but it is the core concept when it comes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 210.59,
          "end": 213.163,
          "en": "to re usability in Vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 214.47,
          "end": 216.55,
          "en": "But, it doesn't stop there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 216.55,
          "end": 218.48,
          "en": "That is something we learnt thus far.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 218.48,
          "end": 222.07,
          "en": "Now here's the new part, even with components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 222.07,
          "end": 224.87,
          "en": "which are great for having an encapsulated template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 224.87,
          "end": 227.8,
          "en": "and logic, customization options with props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 227.8,
          "end": 231.32,
          "en": "and custom events and slots, even with those components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 231.32,
          "end": 233.6,
          "en": "And even with this powerful concept,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 233.6,
          "end": 236.61,
          "en": "we sometimes are left with some code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 236.61,
          "end": 238.6,
          "en": "which we would want to reuse,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 238.6,
          "end": 241.58,
          "en": "but which be conscientious as easily.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 241.58,
          "end": 244.75,
          "en": "Because what if we have queue components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 244.75,
          "end": 249.34,
          "en": "that have related or similar logic in them, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 249.34,
          "end": 252.36,
          "en": "the user list component with a search method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 252.36,
          "end": 256.1,
          "en": "data related to search and a Watcher related to search.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 256.1,
          "end": 259.11,
          "en": "And then we have to same logic in another component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 260.33,
          "end": 263.83,
          "en": "in such cases, creating a new component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 263.83,
          "end": 268.44,
          "en": "which has this combined logic might not always be possible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 268.44,
          "end": 271.4,
          "en": "and therefore when using the options API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 271.4,
          "end": 273.86,
          "en": "you have a concept called mixins,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 273.86,
          "end": 277.63,
          "en": "which basically allows you to share data, methods,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 277.63,
          "end": 281.27,
          "en": "computed properties, Watchers, lifecycle hooks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 281.27,
          "end": 285.94,
          "en": "whichever configuration you might need across components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 285.94,
          "end": 288.445,
          "en": "So therefore let's explore mixins",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 288.445,
          "end": 290.48,
          "en": "and let's see how they can help us here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 290.48,
          "end": 292.523,
          "en": "in this example project.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
